// declarations of the member carry the premise. A `quant null-deref` fact does
// not depend on which callback runs and carries none.
//
// Card NULL-MEMBER-INVARIANT-SCOPE (contract specification C09.3, grammar
// G05f, gateway rules 14x-14z): scoped member invariants. `requires
// nonnull_member(TAG, FIELD) where quant #scope [[stable]];` says FIELD is never made NULL on an
// existing struct TAG object: every assignment the analysed units make to it
// is checked non-null (one not proved withdraws the declaration for the
// run), while an initializer list writes a fresh object and may leave it
// NULL. A non-null value seen on an object then stays non-null for that
// object's lifetime, so the null walk keeps a tested or dereferenced
// `V->FIELD` (V a tracked local or formal) across calls and stores. Whole-
// object writes through an untyped pointer stay a listed premise, so the
// declaration is never `validated`.
