// Card NULL-MEMBER-INVARIANT-SCOPE (rule 14z): function-scope entries of the
// registered broker. `requires nonnull_member(rd_kafka_broker_s, rkb_rk,
// rkb) where quant #scope [[scope]];` says the broker `rkb` names has a non-null rkb_rk on entry; every
// caller's actual is a checked obligation, and with rkb_rk stable (above) the
// entry fact lasts the whole body. Chosen by `scripts/scope_candidates.py`
// from the stable reading's run: each function whose own row kept a
// candidate on `rkb->rkb_rk` alone, whose first parameter is the broker,
// whose definition is byte-identical at 66910c10 and 046accf6, whose address
// the library never takes (an indirect caller is never checked), and whose
// parameters all have bounds v1 types. Each comment counts the first reads
// on the stable reading.

// lib/librdkafka-2.15.0/src/rdkafka_fetcher.c: 1 first read(s) of rkb->rkb_rk on the stable reading.
